Author: halamikel <37craven@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 19:52:20 2026 +0800

    Build the collections UI, public profiles and account recovery
    
    Collections and search
    - Collections grid with the server's own tiles, status dropdown offering only
      legal moves, create and delete
    - Collection detail: rows and all four widget types (notes with a working
      checklist, dates, pictures, links with previews), plus sharing
    - One search box for both collections and people, results grouped by type.
      The people request only fires for 2-20 characters, the window the server
      accepts, so a long phrase cannot come back a 400.
    - Row and widget reordering. Both endpoints insist on the COMPLETE id list, so
      a move rebuilds the array rather than sending just the pair that swapped.
    
    Profiles
    - /u/:username for everyone, /profile redirects so old links still work
    - Friend actions on the profile: add, accept, decline, cancel, remove
    - Find people by username, wired to the friend-request endpoints
    
    Accounts
    - Register now waits for a confirmation email instead of signing you in
    - Forgot password, reset password, and confirm-email pages; the login screen
      offers a resend when an account is not yet confirmed
    
    Fixes found while building
    - src/lib/api.ts set a default Content-Type of application/json. Axios
      rewrites FormData into JSON when it sees that, so every upload sent
      {"image":{}} and the server found no file. Removing the one line fixes
      collection pictures, crumbs AND profile photos.
    - Asset URLs were rendered raw, so the browser asked Vite for /uploads/... and
      got index.html back: a 200 with text/html, and an image that silently never
      appeared. One assetUrl() helper now covers card tiles, widget pictures and
      link previews.
    - Sign-out and the friends dialog were only reachable through a page that
      became dead when /profile started redirecting.
    
    lint and build clean.

