Author: halamikel <37craven@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 6 22:22:20 2026 +0800

    Match the frontend to the unified backend
    
    The API moved while these branches were apart, so the client was calling
    endpoints that no longer exist and sending uploads the server can no longer
    read.
    
    - POST /api/crumbs and PUT /api/auth/avatar now send multipart/form-data with
      the picture in a field named "image"; caption and collection go in the body.
      They were raw blobs with query parameters, which the server ignores now.
    - Friends come from /api/friends, not /api/auth/friends.
    - The "?collection=" param nothing implemented is now collectionId in the
      body, and it works: the upload files the photo into that collection too.
    - src/lib/collections.ts fills the picker from GET /api/collections. Profile
      and Crumbs both use it, replacing the hardcoded empty array.
    - An upload whose collection copy is refused reports it instead of silently
      pretending it worked; the crumb itself is still saved.
    - Dropped crumbsCount/collectionsCount from userSchema. Nothing returned them.
      The counts now come from the lists the page already loads.
    - Added deleteCrumb() for the new DELETE route.

